    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The date of the first mosque is unknown, with dates from 1200 to 1330 suggested, and the building seen today was rebuilt in 1906 and 1907 in the colonial period.</li><li>Historians disagree about the French role in the 1907 design: Félix Dubois blamed the colonial administration, while Jean-Louis Bourgeois argued that the design is basically African and that the local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guild</a> of masons built it.</li><li>The whole community of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djenne">Djenné</a> repairs the earth walls each year at a festival, and the town has resisted modernisation of the building in favour of its historical integrity.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The three towers of the qibla wall are topped with cone-shaped pinnacles crowned with ostrich eggs, and the bundles of palm sticks that stud the walls double as built-in scaffolding for the yearly repairs.</p></aside>
    </section>

